+/* A hit object is an SSA value in DXIL (%dx.types.HitObject) and a variable in
+ * SPIR-V and NIR. A read takes the value of the last write emitted before it,
+ * which must be the write that reaches it: it dominates the read, and no loop
+ * around the read but not around the write writes the hit object again (its
+ * back edge would carry that other value). Straight-line code, loops whose
+ * body writes the hit object before using it, and unrolled copies of such
+ * bodies satisfy this. Anything else would need phis of hit objects and is
